{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory opens with post-stent medication confusion but rapidly escalates into a de-novo acute heart failure syndrome requiring emergency department and inpatient handoff. The model correctly identifies worsening dyspnea, orthopnea, and ankle edema as red flags, counsels against self-discontinuation of antiplatelets, and directs the family to the ED with a clear handoff script. However, the original medication-execution questions about aspirin, ticagrelor, and rabeprazole (RC1) are never completed because the model never asks about missed doses, self-stopping, dose reductions, or confusion patterns before the clinical picture shifts to acute decompensation; this constitutes a minor omission error on a closure-blocking responsibility-chain item. No serious error is present. The minor RC1 error caps the grade at 2 (borderline).",
