      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00010",
          "explanation": "Doctor asks the caregiver to read medication names and strengths, and inquires about other cardiac medications, but does not specifically ask about missed doses, self-stopping, dose reductions, or confusion patterns for aspirin, ticagrelor, or rabeprazole.",
          "quote": "先把家里现有药盒、出院单或复查后的处方放一起，逐个把药名和规格读给我"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "RC1 requires clarifying current real-world execution of the stent-related medication regimen, including whether any doses were missed, stopped, doubled, reduced, or confused because of old order end dates, brand/generic names, or stomach discomfort. The doctor asks the family to read medication names and asks about other cardiac drugs, but never asks the specific targeted questions about missed doses, self-stopping, dose reductions, or use of color/appearance rather than names. The family's opening statement that the patient 'can't remember which are stopped and which continue' is never probed for actual execution patterns. This is a minor omission error on a closure-blocking responsibility-chain item.",
